    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物调节免疫治疗的分子与细胞机制\",\n      \"purpose\": \"解析代谢物、免疫细胞互作及抗原模拟等具体生物学路径，明确动物模型证据与人类临床证据的界限，避免将临床前机制直接外推为人类临床事实。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖肠道微生物代谢物（肌苷、短链脂肪酸、色氨酸衍生物、胆汁酸）与宿主受体互作、免疫细胞（DC、T 细胞、髓系细胞）调节机制、抗原模拟假说及细菌易位路径。重点区分小鼠模型因果验证与人类观察性/替代标志物证据。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n          \"reason\": \"主要为 FMT 干预试验临床结局（ORR、安全性），机制线索（SCFA 产生菌）已在 P0092/P0503 中覆盖，归入 Ch5 更宜。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n          \"reason\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果及免疫微环境分析，属干预性证据，归入 Ch5。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0104\",\n          \"reason\": \"主要为 NSCLC 队列微生物特征与 PFS 关联的观察性数据，缺乏具体分子机制，归入 Ch2。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0590\",\n          \"reason\": \"同 P0578，为 MITRIC 试验结果，归入 Ch5。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0591\",\n          \"reason\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验摘要，侧重临床结局与毒性，归入 Ch5。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"代谢物 - 宿主受体轴：从肿瘤内在免疫原性到免疫细胞重编程\",\n          \"argument\": \"微生物代谢物通过不同路径调节 ICI 疗效：肌苷直接作用于肿瘤细胞（UBA6 抑制）增强免疫原性，而 SCFAs、色氨酸衍生物及胆汁酸主要通过免疫细胞受体（HDAC、AhR、GPCR）调节功能。人类证据中，肌苷 -UBA6 轴有血浆分层及肿瘤 UBA6 表达验证（n=22），但 SCFAs 等缺乏肿瘤微环境绝对浓度数据，多为粪便关联或小鼠模型。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0582\",\n            \"P0092\",\n            \"P0503\",\n            \"P0515\",\n            \"P0518\",\n            \"P0559\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_boundary\": \"肌苷在 CheckMate 025 队列有人类血浆分层数据（高肌苷组 OS 33 个月 vs 22 个月），但 UBA6 验证队列仅 n=22 且未测血浆肌苷；SCFAs 人类数据多为粪便浓度与 PFS 关联，缺乏 TME 内浓度及因果验证。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"先天 - 适应性免疫桥接：树突状细胞成熟与 T 细胞启动\",\n          \"argument\": \"特定菌群（如 Ruminococcaceae、Bifidobacterium）通过 TLR/STING 通路促进 DC 成熟及迁移至引流淋巴结，增强 CD8+ T 细胞启动。细菌易位（如 E. faecalis）至 MLN 及肿瘤组织是连接肠道与远端免疫的关键物理路径，但在人类中多为检测到的关联，因果链主要在小鼠 FMT 模型中证实。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0114\",\n            \"P0166\",\n            \"P0009\",\n            \"P0388\",\n            \"P0506\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_boundary\": \"DC 迁移及 T 细胞启动机制多基于无菌小鼠及 FMT 模型；人类证据多为肿瘤组织免疫浸润（CD8+ T 细胞）与特定菌丰度的相关性，缺乏动态示踪证据。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"抗原模拟与交叉反应：体液与细胞免疫的双重假说\",\n          \"argument\": \"微生物肽段与肿瘤新抗原序列同源（分子模拟）可诱导交叉反应性 T 细胞或抗体（如抗糖脂抗体），增强抗肿瘤免疫。该机制解释了部分非代谢依赖的疗效关联，但目前多为生物信息学预测或小样本免疫组库分析，缺乏大规模临床队列的功能性验证。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0037\",\n            \"P0190\",\n            \"P0561\",\n            \"P0570\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_boundary\": \"分子模拟主要为假说或计算预测，人类 T 细胞交叉反应性证据有限；抗糖脂抗体机制为新兴假说，尚未成为共识。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"证据局限与情境依赖：种属差异、浓度缺口及肿瘤异质性\",\n          \"argument\": \"机制研究多依赖小鼠模型，人类验证受限于样本获取（TME 代谢物难测）及混杂因素（饮食、药物）。同一代谢物（如丁酸盐）在不同肿瘤类型或 ICI 靶点下可能具有双向作用，需避免单一机制的普适化断言。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0582\",\n            \"P0092\",\n            \"P0503\",\n            \"P0589\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_boundary\": \"缺乏人体 TME 代谢物绝对浓度阈值；小鼠模型中有效的机制（如特定菌株定植）在人类中受定植抵抗限制；代谢物效应在 PD-1 vs CTLA-4 及不同癌种间存在不一致性。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [\n        {\n          \"gap_id\": \"human_metabolite_concentration\",\n          \"gap_question\": \"人体肿瘤微环境或配对血清中肌苷及短链脂肪酸的具体生理浓度是多少，且是否与 ICI 响应直接相关？\",\n          \"success_criteria\": \"找到至少一项研究，报告了人类实体瘤患者 TME 或血清中肌苷/SCFAs 的绝对浓度（μM/ng/mL），并提供了与 ORR/PFS 的统计关联。\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"用于 Ch3 中明确人类证据的定量缺口，纠正将小鼠模型浓度直接外推至人类的过度断言。\",\n          \"targeted_queries\": [\n            \"human tumor microenvironment inosine concentration immune checkpoint inhibitor response\",\n            \"human serum short-chain fatty acids concentration PD-1 blockade efficacy\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"gap_id\": \"uba6_human_expression\",\n          \"gap_question\": \"UBA6 蛋白在人体多种实体瘤中的表达谱及其与 ICI 疗效的大队列验证数据是否存在？\",\n          \"success_criteria\": \"找到除 P0582 中 n=22 队列外，更大规模的人类肿瘤队列 UBA6 表达与 ICI 疗效的关联数据。\",\n          \"intended_use\": \"用于评估肌苷 -UBA6 轴作为通用机制的可靠性，支持 Ch3 中关于人类验证有限的论点。\",\n          \"targeted_queries\": [\n            \"UBA6 protein expression human solid tumors immune checkpoint inhibitor outcome\",\n            \"UBA6 prognostic biomarker cancer immunotherapy large cohort\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0503\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0563\"\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"承接 Ch2 中观察到的微生物 - 疗效关联（如 Akkermansia、SCFAs），本章深入解析其背后的生物学路径（如 UBA6 抑制、HDAC 抑制），为 Ch4 讨论情境因素（如饮食、抗生素如何改变这些代谢物水平）及 Ch5 评估干预策略（如补充代谢物 vs FMT）提供机制依据。需明确 Ch2 的关联不等于 Ch3 的因果机制，特别是人类数据的局限性。\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants a chapter proposal for \"Ch3_Mechanisms\" of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nI need to structure the response as a JSON object containing `chapter_proposals` and `screened_sources`.\nThe chapter proposal must include:\n- `chapter_id`: \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n- `title`: \"微生物调节免疫治疗的分子与细胞机制\" (Microbial Molecular and Cellular Mechanisms Regulating Immunotherapy)\n- `purpose`: Explain metabolic, immune cell interaction, and antigen mimicry pathways, distinguishing animal model evidence from human clinical evidence.\n- `scope`: Focus on specific biological pathways (Inosine-UBA6, SCFAs, Tryptophan derivatives), immune cell types (DCs, CD8+ T cells), and evidence boundaries (preclinical vs. human).\n- `substantive_threads`: Ordered themes for the chapter.\n- `supplement_requests`: Gaps needing further search (e.g., specific metabolite concentrations in human TME).\n- `directed_reads`: Specific sources to read deeply if needed (though source_routing is already done, I should reference specific handles for key arguments).\n- `excluded_source_handles`: Sources routed to this chapter but deemed out of scope for *this specific chapter's argument* (e.g., purely clinical association without mechanism, or purely intervention without mechanism).\n- `transition_logic`: How this chapter connects to Ch2 (Clinical Associations) and Ch4 (Contextual Factors).\n\nI need to use the provided `source_routing` information to select relevant sources for this chapter.\nKey sources routed to Ch3_Mechanisms include: P0009, P0114, P0196, P0447, P0503, P0582, CorpusId:252309032 (which corresponds to P0582 based on the title \"Inhibition of UBA6 by inosine...\").\nI also see many other sources routed to Ch3_Mechanisms in the `source_routing` list (e.g., P0002, P0004, P0005, P0009, P0013, P0014, P0017, P0018, P0021, P0022, P0023, P00